Part 1: SBIR Phase I Technical Abstract

Project Title: High-Velocity 1000Hz Active Inference Cybernetic Architecture for Low-Latency Robotic Command and Control
Company Name: Krypticsoundz LLC
Principal Investigator: Brandon Mark Wilson
Technical Abstract:
Current autonomous robotic systems and unmanned edge platforms are fundamentally bottlenecked by the processing latency and non-deterministic timing of traditional middleware architectures and optimization loops. Classical control algorithms often experience significant tracking drift and sensory-motor desynchronization when subjected to rapid kinetic stressors, high transient vibrations, or dense sensor data streams.
To resolve this critical operational gap, Krypticsoundz LLC proposes the development of Kryptic-Agent, a high-velocity, bare-metal active inference robotics framework engineered to deliver deterministic 1000Hz sensory-motor corrections. The innovation shifts away from standard abstract reinforcement models, utilizing direct real-time minimization of Variational Free Energy (VFE) matrix loops implemented on bare-metal physical interfaces. By coupling native ROS 2 physical driver bindings with optimized Eclipse Cyclone DDS transport mechanics, the software ensures sub-millisecond multi-axis actuation tracking and homeostatic stability.
Phase I research will focus on the technical feasibility of executing continuous VFE matrix minimization at a deterministic 1000Hz clock cadence on low-power, edge-embedded hardware controllers. The project will evaluate system tracking accuracy, homeostatic check latencies under simulated 50G transient vibration stressors, and real-time data ingestion integrity via hard real-time POSIX scheduling. Successful verification will establish a hardened, dual-use middleware suite prepared for Phase II deployment across autonomous military fleets, tactical drone swarms, and advanced commercial industrial automation.
Anticipated Benefits and Commercial Applications:
• Defense: Provides a lightweight, high-speed, secure command and control layer for autonomous ground stations, tactical unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), and edge robotic systems operating in contested, high-vibration, or electronically degraded environments.
• Commercial: Delivers ultra-low latency middleware for high-precision manufacturing, industrial robotic arms, automated distribution logistics, and commercial drone fleet coordination requiring real-time mechanical error mitigation.
